      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "This issue is still 100% present, if another user joins the instance you are in the \"Reset Config\" button under the OSC menu ceases to function and you must rejoin the instance or move to another one to get the configuration file to regenerate. This causes the authors of a lot of OSC apps to manually delete configs in the OSC folder under AppData to get the configs to regenerate when uploading a new version of an avatar: https://docs.hai-vr.dev/docs/products/auto-reset-osc-config\n\nI think this behavior should be automatic whenever an updated version of an avatar is loaded, if you're concerned about overwriting custom configs then just use an example config like was discussed here: https://feedback.vrchat.com/feature-requests/p/dont-write-the-osc-config-by-default",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
